{"uid":"10283e9973dfcb5b","name":"test_build_with_ai_skill_auto_attaches_and_redirects_to_agent","fullName":"tests.ui.agents.test_build_with_ai_skill_from_agent.TestBuildWithAISkillFromAgent#test_build_with_ai_skill_auto_attaches_and_redirects_to_agent","historyId":"e715a746976621fa73c6743928afa012","time":{"start":1787301255269,"stop":1787301310120,"duration":54851},"description":"Creating a Skill via Build with AI from an Agent's SKILLS section\n        redirects back to the Agent editor (never the Skill details page),\n        auto-attaches the new Skill once the async attach chain completes,\n        and the attachment persists after Save + reload.\n\n        Steps (AFS\n        test-specs/agents/l2_build-with-ai-skill-from-agent-auto-attaches-and-redirects_ELITEA-1999.md):\n        1. Open the fixture Agent for editing; in the SKILLS section click\n           \"+ Skill\" -> \"Create new\"; verify navigation to\n           /skills/create?source_application_id=...&return_url=....\n        2. Click \"Build with AI\"; fill the prompt; click Generate; verify\n           the generate-draft POST resolves 200 and the review form shows\n           the generated Name/Description/Instructions.\n        3. Click \"Create Skill\"; verify the creation POST resolves 201 and\n           the URL transitions to /agents/all/{agent_id}?..., NOT to a\n           Skill-details URL.\n        4. Verify the user lands on the Agent editor, not the Skill details\n           page.\n        5. Verify the new Skill is automatically attached (async — poll,\n           do not assert immediately, see SKILL_ATTACH_TIMEOUT).\n        6. Save the Agent and reload it; verify the attached Skill is still\n           present and correctly linked.\n        ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Creating a Skill via Build with AI from an Agent's SKILLS section<br />\nredirects back to the Agent editor (never the Skill details page),<br />\nauto-attaches the new Skill once the async attach chain completes,<br />\nand the attachment persists after Save + reload.</p>\n<pre><code>    Steps (AFS\n    test-specs/agents/l2_build-with-ai-skill-from-agent-auto-attaches-and-redirects_ELITEA-1999.md):\n    1. Open the fixture Agent for editing; in the SKILLS section click\n       &quot;+ Skill&quot; -&gt; &quot;Create new&quot;; verify navigation to\n       /skills/create?source_application_id=...&amp;return_url=....\n    2. Click &quot;Build with AI&quot;; fill the prompt; click Generate; verify\n       the generate-draft POST resolves 200 and the review form shows\n       the generated Name/Description/Instructions.\n    3. Click &quot;Create Skill&quot;; verify the creation POST resolves 201 and\n       the URL transitions to /agents/all/{agent_id}?..., NOT to a\n       Skill-details URL.\n    4. Verify the user lands on the Agent editor, not the Skill details\n       page.\n    5. Verify the new Skill is automatically attached (async — poll,\n       do not assert immediately, see SKILL_ATTACH_TIMEOUT).\n    6. Save the Agent and reload it; verify the attached Skill is still\n       present and correctly linked.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"failed","statusMessage":"AssertionError: Expected the Skills counter to read \"1/N skills added.\" once the async attach chain completes, got '0/5 skills added.'\nassert False\n +  where False = <built-in method startswith of str object at 0x7ffa66bd54d0>('1/')\n +    where <built-in method startswith of str object at 0x7ffa66bd54d0> = '0/5 skills added.'.startswith","statusTrace":"tests/ui/agents/test_build_with_ai_skill_from_agent.py:217: in test_build_with_ai_skill_auto_attaches_and_redirects_to_agent\n    assert counter_text.startswith(\"1/\"), (\nE   AssertionError: Expected the Skills counter to read \"1/N skills added.\" once the async attach chain completes, got '0/5 skills added.'\nE   assert False\nE    +  where False = <built-in method startswith of str object at 0x7ffa66bd54d0>('1/')\nE    +    where <built-in method startswith of str obj